    {
      "id": "claim_4936b41d831c4e399edbec7aa10dc678",
      "statement": "Dirty registries (psChanges, rsChanges) coalesce multiple edits of the same row into a single entry per row, with field-level changedFields and an earliest `before` snapshot used for staleness checks. Persisted to SQLite (pending_changes table) so browser crashes never lose queued work. On project reopen, registries are restored and re-merged onto freshly parsed rows via natural keys.",
